      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 IOP Publishing Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "We investigate spin-dependent electronic states of antiferromagnetic (AFM) lanthanum chromite (LaCrO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;), lanthanum manganite (LaMnO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;), and lanthanum ferrite (LaFeO&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;) using spin-polarized first-principles density functional theory (DFT) with Hubbard &lt;i&gt;U&lt;/i&gt; correction. The band structures are calculated for 15 types of their different AFM structures. It is verified for these structures that there is a very simple rule to identify which wave number &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;k&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; exhibits spin splitting or degeneracy in the band structure. This rule uses the symmetry operations that map the up-spin atoms onto the down-spin atoms. The resulting spin splitting is very small for the most stable spin configuration of the most stable experimental structure. We discuss a plausible benefit of this characteristic, &lt;i&gt;i.e.&lt;/i&gt;, the direction-independence of the spin current, in electrode applications."
      },
